$DATUM (3R)-6-bromo-8-(1H-indol-5-yl)-7-methyl-5-oxo-2,3-dihydro-5H-thiazolo[3,2-a]pyridine-3-
carboxylic acid methyl ester (8g) A mixture of
(3R)-6-bromo-8-iodo-7-methyl-5-oxo-2,3-dihydro-5H-thiazolo[3,2-a]pyridine-
3-carboxylic acid methyl ester (20mg, 0.047mmol), 1H-indol-5-ylboronic
acid (8mg, 0.047mmol), PEPPSI-iPr (1.5mg, 0.0024mmol) and KF (5mg,
0.094mmol) in dry MeOH (dried over 3Å MS) was heated in the microwave
oven att 120°C for 10min. The reaction was diluted with saturated NaHCO3
and extracted with EtOAc (30ml), the organic phase was dried (Na2SO4),
filtered and concentrated. The crude product was purified with column
chromatography on silica gel (heptane:EtOAc 1:1). The title compound vas
isolated as a colorless foam (16mg, 83% yield): [α]D -76 (c0.5, CHCl3).
IR λ 3274, 1747, 1627, 1569, 1472, 1217. 1H-NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.38
(bs, 1H), 7.43-7.53 (m, 2H), 7.27-7.31 (m, 1H), 6.98-7.05 (m, 1H),
6.57-6.61 (m, 1H), 5.68-5.74 (m, 1H), 3.84 and 3.83 (s, 3H), 3.60- 3.68
(m, 1H), 3.42 (dd, J = 11.8, 2.5 Hz, 1H), 2.17 (s, 3H). 13C-NMR (100MHz,
CDCl3) δ 168.6 (splitted), 157.7, 151.7, 145.6 and 145.5 (1C), 135.7 and
135.6 (1C), 128.6 and 128.5 (1C), 128.3 and 128.2 (1C), 125.4 and 125.3
(1C), 123.9 and 123.5 (1C), 122.4 and 122.1 (1C), 117.7 (splitted), 112.5
(splitted), 111.8 and 111.7 (1C), 103.1 and 103.0 (1C), 65.0 and 64.9
(1C), 53.6 and 53.5 (1C), 31.8 (splitted), 22.5. HRMS (ES+) calcd [M+H+]
C18H15BrN2O3S, 419.0065, obsd 419.0064
