$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedures for iodination of 2 and
subsequent Suzuki coupling: A solution of compound 2 (1 mmol) and
N-iodosuccinimide (NIS) (1.05 mmol) in acetone (15 mL) was stirred at
room temperature (rt) for 3 hours (h). Saturated aqueous sodium
thiosulfate (5 mL) was added. After stirring for 5 minutes (min), ethyl
acetate (30 mL) and water (20 mL) were added. Layers were separated. The
aqueous solution was extracted with ethyl acetate (2 x 25 mL). The
combined organic layer was washed with brine, dried over magnesium
sulfate and concentrated in vacuo to give the crude product. To the
suspension of this crude 3-iodoindole (1.0 mmol) product and
[1,1'-bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene] dichloropalladium (PdCl2(dppf)2 )
(0.1 mmol) in dimethoxyethane (DME) (12 mL) at rt was added a solution of
2-methoxypyridine 3-boronic acid (1.2 mmol) and potassium carbonate (5.0
mmol) in water (3.0 mL). The mixture was bubbled with argon gas through a
frit glass bubbler for 5 min before it was heated to 90 ºC in an oil bath
and stirred for 4 h. After cooled to rt, the mixture was diluted with
water and ethyl acetate (30 mL each) and the two layers were separated.
The aqueous solution was extracted with ethyl acetate (2 x 20 mL). The
combined organic solution was washed with brine, dried over magnesium
sulfate and concentrated in vacuo to give the crude product, which was
purified by silica gel flash chromatography using 0-50% ethyl acetate in
hexanes as eluent.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling in stage 3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of SCH 900188: A Potent Hepatitis C Virus NS5B Polymerase
Inhibitor Prodrug As a Development Candidate
