$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3. General procedure for Suzuki-Miyaura
coupling of heteroaryl chlorides with aryl/heteroarylboron reagents.
Under argon atmosphere, a reaction tube was charged with palladium salt
(Pd(OAc)2 (2.25 mg, 0.01 mmol) or [Pd(allyl)Cl]2 (1.83 mg, 0.005 mmol)),
imidazolium salt 2d (8.66 mg, 0.02 mmol) and cesium carbonate (652 mg, 2
mmol). Then, dioxane (2 mL) was added. The mixture was stirred for 15 min
at 90 °C and cooled to room temperature. (This precatalyst formation was
essential for high catalytic performance.) Then, heteroaryl chloride 3
(1.0 mmol) and (hetero)arylboron reagent 4 (1.5 mmol) were added. The
reaction mixture was stirred for 18 h at 90 °C and cooled to room
temperature. Water and saturated Na2CO3 were added and then the resulting
mixture was extracted with ether. The combined organic layers were dried
over Na2SO4. Concentration and purification through silica gel column
chromatography gave desired product 5. 4-Methoxybiphenyl4 (5aa). Column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc = 100/1) gave the product
3-(5-Acetylthiophen-2-yl)-9-phenylcarbazole (5hl). Column chromatography
(hexane/EtOAc = 5/1) gave the product Yellow solids, 312 mg, (0.85 mmol,
85%). mp 157-158 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): 2.59 (3H, s), 7.31-7.35
(1H, m), 7.38-7.47 (4H, m), 7.50 (1H, t, J = 7.8 Hz), 7.56-7.58 (2H, m),
7.62 (1H, d, J = 7.8 Hz), 7.63 (1H, t, J = 7.8 Hz), 7.70-7.72 (2H, m),
8.18 (1H, d, J = 7.8 Hz), 8.43 (1H, d, J = 1.2 Hz). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): 26.4 (CH3), 110.0 (CH), 110.2 (CH), 118.1 (CH), 120.4 (CH), 122.8
(CH), 123.0 (C), 123.8 (C), 124.4 (CH), 125.4 (C), 126.5 (CH), 126.9
(CH), 127.7 (CH), 129.9 (CH), 133.7 (CH), 137.1 (C), 141.1 (C), 141.4
(C), 141.9 (C), 154.2 (C), 190.4 (C). IR (ATR): 800, 1230, 1440, 1640
cm-1. HRMS (EI) m/z calcd for C24H17NOS (M+): 367.1031. Found: 367.1045.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM catalyst prepared and used (ligand prepared and used), Suzuki-Miyaura
cross coupling
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Ether-Imidazolium Carbenes for Suzuki-Miyaura Cross-Coupling of
Heteroaryl Chlorides with Aryl/Heteroarylboron Reagents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
