$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Synthesis of 3-Aryl-5-bromopyridines
(5). A mixture of 5-bromo-3-iodopyridin-2-amine (1.0 equiv), arylboronic
acid (1.0 equiv), and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.12 equiv) was added to a sealed tube.
The tube was evacuated and backfilled with argon (3 cycles). Acetonitrile
and DMF (3:1 mL) were added by syringe at room temperature, followed by
(1 M) aqueous Na2CO3 (2.0 equiv). After being stirred at 90 °C for about
8 h, the reaction mixture was filtered and concentrated. The residue was
purified by flash column chromatography.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki coupling reaction
