$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of 9. Compound 8 (0.2000 g, 0.36 mmol 1.0 equiv), compound 5
(0.3010 g, 1.07 mmol, 3.0 equiv), K2CO3 (0.2100 g, 1.52 mmol, 4.2 equiv),
and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.0328 g, 28.38 μmol, 0.08 equiv) were added in THF (10
mL) and water (2 mL) under argon. The mixture was stirred at 100 °C for
15 h. After being quenched with water, the reaction mixture was extracted
with chloroform (3 × 25mL) and finally dried over anhydrous MgSO4. After
the solvent was removed in vacuo, the residue was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel with petroleum ether (60-90 °C) as eluent. 9
(0.1870 g, 85%) as a white solid. Mp: 66-68 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz):
δ 7.32 (s, 1H), 7.13 (d, J = 0.8 Hz, 1H), 7.12 (d, J = 0.8 Hz, 1H), 7.11
(s, 1H), 6.88 (d, J = 0.8 Hz, 1H), 6.86 (d, J = 0.8 Hz, 1H), 0.34 (s,
9H), 0.32 (s, 9H), 0.21 (s, 9H), 0.20 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 141.70, 139.93, 139.67, 139.27, 137.98, 137.81, 137.74, 137.57, 136.19,
135.56, 135.05, 134.24, 134.10, 131.31, 127.00, 126.44, -0.05, -0.12,
-0.14, -0.19. IR (KBr): 2956, 2926, 2898, 2855(C-H) cm-1. HRMS
(MALDI/DHB): m/z calcd for [C28H42Si4S4] 618.1247, found 618.1241.
