$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM To a solution of 2-[(4-iodo-yl)methoxy]ethytrimethysilane (1.000 g, 3.08
mmol; see Bioorg. Med. Chem. Lett. 2004, 14, 3063) in acetonitrile (23
mL) was added
2-(1,4-dioxaspiro[4.5]dec-8-en-8-yl)-4,4,5,5-tetramethy1,3,2-dioxaborolane;
1.30 equiv.; 4.009 mmol, commercial), sodium carbonate (493 mg, 1.50
equiv., 4.62 mmol), tetrakistriphenylphosphinepalladium(0) (184 mg, 0.050
equiv., 0.1542 mmol) and deoxygenated water (13 mL). The mixture was
heated to 90 °C and stirred for 3 days. The mixture was diluted with
water, extracted 3X with EtOAc, then the combined organic extracts were
dried (MgSO4)and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by CombiFlash (40 g;
100:0 to 70:30 heptane:EtOAc)provided
2-[[4-(1,4-dioxaspiro[4.5]dec-8-en-8-yl)-yl]methoxy]ethytrimethysilane.
Yield 881 mg, 2.62 mmol, 85%.
