$DATUM (3R)-6-bromo-8-(1H-indol-5-yl)-7-naphthalen-1-ylmethyl-5-oxo-2,3-dihydro-5H-thiazolo[
3,2-a]pyridine-3-carboxylic acid methyl ester (8h) A mixture of
(3R)-6-bromo-8-iodo-7-naphthalen-1-ylmethyl-5-oxo-2,3-dihydro-5Hthiazolo[
3,2-a]pyridine-3-carboxylic acid methyl ester (50mg, 0.09mmol),
1H-indol-5- ylboronic acid (15mg, 0.09mmol), PEPPSI-iPr (3mg, 0.0045mmol)
and KF (10mg, 0.18mmol) in dry MeOH (1.2ml, dried over 3Å MS), was heated
in the microwave oven at 110°C for 10min. The reaction mixture was
diluted with saturated NaHCO3 and extracted with EtOAc (30ml), the
organic phase was dried (Na2SO4), filtered and concentrated. The crude
product was purified with column chromatography on silica gel
(heptane:EtOAc 55:45). The title compound was isolated as a mixture of
two atropo isomers (30mg, 61% yield): [α]D -154 (c0.5, CHCl3). IR λ 1749,
1635, 1468. 1H-NMR (400MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.32 (bs, 1H), 7.77-7.82 (m, 1H),
7.66-7.73 (m, 2H), 7.28-7.44 (m, 4H), 7.05-7.17 (m, 3H), 6.74- 6.87 (m,
1H), 6.30-6.44 (m, 1H), 5.74-5.81 (m, 1H), 4.26-4.43 (m, 2H), 3.86 and
3.85 (s, 3H), 3.64-3.73 (m, 1H), 3.45 (dd, J = 11.8, 2.6 Hz, 1H). 13C-NMR
(100MHz, CDCl3) δ 168.5 and 168.4 (1C), 158.0 (splitted), 153.2 and 153.1
(1C), 146.9 and 146.7 (1C), 135.7 and 135.6 (1C), 133.7 (splitted), 133.1
(splitted), 131.8, 128.7 (splitted), 128.0 (splitted), 127.9 and 127.7
(1C), 127.0 (splitted), 125.9 (splitted), 125.6 (2C, splitted), 125.1
(splitted), 124.5 (splitted), 123.6 and 122.9 (1C), 123.1 (splitted),
122.3 and 121.7 (1C), 118.5 and 118.4 (1C), 114.3 and 114.2 (1C), 111.5
(splitted), 102.9, 65.3 and 65.2 (1C), 53.6 (splitted), 37.5 and 37.4
(1C), 31.8 (splitted), HRMS (ES+) calcd [M+H+] C28H21BrN2O3S, 545.0535,
obsd 545.0531
