$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Compound 4. A mixture of compound 2a (240 mg, 0.3 mmol), 4-pyridylboronic
acid (120 mg, 1 mmol), Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (40 mg, 0.06 mmol), and Cs2CO3 (200
mg, 0.62 mmol) was added to a 5 mL microwave vial. The reactor was
sealed, evacuated, and purged with N2. Then DMF (2.5 mL) and water (0.5
mL) were successively added. The reactor was subjected to microwave
irradiation at 120 °C for 30 min. The resulting mixture was poured into
water (10 mL) and extracted with CH2Cl2 (20 mL). The volatile was
evaporated by rotavapor, and the residue was subjected to column
chromatography on neutral alumina, eluting with 100:5
CH2Cl2/triethylamine, to afford a yellow solid product (180 mg, 85%):
Compound 4. Yield 180 mg, 85% mp 92-94 °C; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.77
(d, J = 6.0 Hz, 4H), 7.51 (d, J = 6.0 Hz, 4H), 3.45 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 8H),
1.64 (m, 8H), 1.26 (m, 24H), 0.88 (t, J = 6.4 Hz, 12H); 13C NMR (75.4
MHz, CDCl3) δ 163.7, 149.5, 142.9, 139.2, 125.1, 120.7, 116.3, 112.1,
61.2, 50.1, 31.5, 28.5, 26.1, 22.5, 13.9; HRMS, ESI (positive) calcd for
[C46H61N6O2]+ 729.4851, found 729.4857.
