$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of
6-(4,4,5,5-Tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)benzo[d][1,3]-dioxole-5-carbonitrile
(3T): Compound 5T (2.29 g, 10 mmol, 1.0 equiv), Bis(pinacolato)diboron
(3.04 g, 12 mmol, 1.2 equiv), PdCl2(dppf) (0.22 g, 0.3 mmol, 3 mol %) and
KOAc (2.8 g, 30 mmol, 3.0 equiv) were dissolved in dry 1,4-dioxane (25
mL) in a one-neck round bottom flask (50-mL). The reaction mixture was
kept stirring at 80 °C for 36 h. The crude reaction mixture was diluted
with CH2Cl2, extracted by NaHCO3. The combined organic layer was
collected, dried over the MgSO4 and concentrated in vacuo then purified
after re-crystallization under hexane. Corresponding product 3T as a pale
yellow solid (2.32 g, 85%). Mp: 149–151 °C; 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3): δ
7.27 (s, 1H), 7.09 (s, 1H), 6.06 (s, 2H), 1.36 (s, 12H); 13C NMR (150
MHz, CDCl3): δ 150.4, 149.8, 118.8, 113.2, 111.0, 102.2, 84.7, 24.8;
HRMS: C14H16BNO4 calculated 273.1172, found 273.1165.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydride-Induced Anionic Cyclization: An Efficient Method for the
Synthesis of 6-H-Phenanthridines via a Transition-Metal-Free Process
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
