$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for the palladium-catalyzed
Miyaura borylation: To a solution of appropriate bromoindole (1 equiv) in
dioxane anhydrous (2 ml x mmol) under N2, were added Pd2(dba)3 (0.02
equiv), XPhos (2-dicyclohexylphosphino-2',4',6'-triisopropylbiphenyl)
(0.04 equiv), KOAc (3 equiv) e bis(pinacolato)diboron (1.2 equiv). The
reaction mixture was stirred at 110 °C for 20 hours under N2, then was
cooled at room temperature, filtrate over Celite and washed with ethyl
acetate. To the reaction mixture was added water. The layers were
separated and the aqueous phase was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 x (3
ml x mmol)). The combined organic phases were washed with brine, dried
over anhydrous sodium sulphate and the solvent evaporated under reduced
pressure. The residue obtained was purified by flash chromatography.
Using 4-bromo-1H-indole (4 g, 20.4 mmol). The residue was purified by
flashchromatography (cyclohexane/CH2Cl2 1:1). Using 5-bromo-1H-indole (4
g, 20.4 mmol). The residue was purified by flashchromatography
(cyclohexane/CH2Cl2 3:7).
5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-indole (1b) as a white
solid, yield 4.2 g, 17.1 mmol, 84%. TLC (cyclohexane/CH2Cl2 3:7), Rf =
0.33 (UV, CAM). MS (ESI): 244[M+H]+. 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.44 (s,
12H), 6.60 (br s, 1H), 7.15 (t, J = 3 Hz, 1H,), 7.37 (d, J = 8 Hz, 1H),
7.72 (d, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 8.29 (s, 1H), 8.42 (br s, 1H). 13C NMR (50 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 25.0, 83.6, 103.0, 110.7, 124.5, 127.7, 128.0, 128.7, 138.0
(carbon adjacent to boron was not observed). 11B NMR (64 MHz, CDCl3
BF3•OEt2): δ 32.0. FTIR (film, cm-1): 3336, 2923, 1610, 1578. M.p.:
93-94°C. Anal. Calcd. for C14H18BNO2 (243.14): C, 69.17; H, 7.46; N,
5.76. Found: C, 69.22; H, 7.41; N, 5.73.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Miyaura borylation
